    <h2 id="section-1">1. General</h2>

    <details>
        <summary>What is WetWijzer?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>WetWijzer is an unofficial search and information platform for Belgian legislation. It offers searchable databases of laws, decrees, ordinances, case law and parliamentary documents, supplemented by an AI chatbot that answers questions about Belgian law.</p>
            <p>The service is also available as <a href="https://lisloi.be">LisLoi</a> (French) and <a href="https://gesetzguide.be">GesetzGuide</a> (German) and <a href="https://lexlibera.be">LexLibera</a> (English).</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Is WetWijzer an official government initiative?</summary>
        <div><p>No. WetWijzer is independent of the Belgian government, the judiciary, the Belgian Bar Associations and all other official bodies. The information on the platform originates from public sources such as the Belgian Official Gazette, Justel, Reflex, JuPortal and EUR-Lex.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Is the information on WetWijzer legal advice?</summary>
        <div><p><strong>No.</strong> All information on WetWijzer, including responses from the AI chatbot, is provided for general informational purposes only. No attorney-client relationship is created. Always consult a qualified lawyer for your specific situation.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Is WetWijzer free to use?</summary>
        <div><p>Searching the legislation database is entirely free and requires no account. Upon registration you receive <strong><%= RegistrationsController::STARTER_CREDITS %> free starter credits</strong>. Additional credits can be purchased, or you can subscribe to WetWijzer Pro for extended functionality.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>In which languages is WetWijzer available?</summary>
        <div><p>The interface is available in Dutch, French, German and English. The AI chatbot responds in the language you select. The legislation database contains texts in their original publication language.</p></div>
    </details>

    <h2 id="section-2">2. Account and registration</h2>

    <details>
        <summary>Do I need an account?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>Searching the legislation database does not require an account. An account is required to use the chatbot. An account is needed to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Purchase credits</li>
                <li>Subscribe to WetWijzer Pro</li>
                <li>Save bookmarks</li>
                <li>Permanently store preferences</li>
                <li>Save conversations to your profile</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What information is required for registration?</summary>
        <div><p>Only an email address and password. Your name is optional. We do not ask for phone number, address or any other personal data.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>How do I delete my account?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>You can delete your account via the account page. After confirmation, your account will be scheduled for permanent deletion after 30 days. During this period, you can contact us to cancel the deletion. After 30 days, all personal data is irreversibly erased.</p>
            <p>Unused credits are not refunded upon deletion.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What happens if I do not confirm my email?</summary>
        <div><p>Unconfirmed accounts are automatically deleted after 72 hours. You can re-register afterwards.</p></div>
    </details>

    <h2 id="section-3">3. AI chatbot</h2>

    <details>
        <summary>How does the AI chatbot work?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>The chatbot uses Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG): your question is first matched against the Belgian legislation database to find relevant legal articles, then a large language model (LLM) formulates a response based on those sources.</p>
            <p>This improves accuracy compared to a standard chatbot, but does not eliminate all risks of inaccuracy.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What are the intelligence levels?</summary>
        <div>
            <%= render 'legal_pages/chatbot_pricing_table', locale: :en %>
            <p>New users receive <%= RegistrationsController::STARTER_CREDITS %> free starter credits. Genius, Mastermind and Omniscient are exclusive to Pro subscribers.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>How is reasoning depth determined?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>The available choices depend on the selected model. Mistral Small 4 offers Fast and Deep; models whose providers support three distinct efforts also offer Balanced. The configured surcharges are <strong><%= chatbot_reasoning_surcharge_list %> credits</strong>. A surcharge is charged only when that model supports and uses the selected mode, and the exact total is shown before you send the question.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Can I trust the chatbot responses?</summary>
        <div>
            <p><strong>No, not without verification.</strong> The AI chatbot may:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Present incorrect information as fact ("hallucinations")</li>
                <li>Cite outdated legislation</li>
                <li>Misinterpret legal concepts</li>
                <li>Reference non-existent laws or articles</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Always verify responses against official sources or consult a legal professional. The brilliant level generally provides more accurate answers than the simple level.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What is the difference between the chatbot and Google?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>The WetWijzer chatbot is specifically connected to the Belgian legislation database. Unlike a generic search engine:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>The chatbot searches the full text of Belgian laws, decrees and ordinances directly</li>
                <li>The chatbot cites specific legal articles with source references</li>
                <li>The chatbot formulates a coherent answer instead of a list of links</li>
                <li>The case law and parliamentary databases on the site are free for everyone to browse; via the chatbot, case law and parliamentary documents are available to Pro subscribers</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Are my chatbot conversations stored?</summary>
        <div>
            <p><strong>By default, we do not save your conversations.</strong> If you enable history with a storage password, the saved copy is encrypted in your browser (zero-knowledge AES-256-GCM) before transmission, and we cannot decrypt it without that password. If you save history without a storage password, it is encrypted on our server, but we manage the key and can read the saved content.</p>
            <p>Your current question and relevant recent context are always processed temporarily in readable form by WetWijzer, Azure OpenAI for retrieval (and, in Deep search, optionally Mistral Small for HyDE expansion), and the selected answer provider. No unencrypted conversation content is stored in <code>localStorage</code> or <code>sessionStorage</code>.</p>
            <p>Our analytics database records account-linked pseudonymous usage metadata (such as legal domain, language, model, credits, cost and response time), but no readable question text or question fingerprint.</p>
            <p>See our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy (section 3.4)</a> for full details.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Where are my questions processed?</summary>
        <div><p><%= chatbot_processing_location_summary(:en) %></p></div>
    </details>

    <h2 id="section-4">4. Credits and payments</h2>

    <details>
        <summary>What are credits?</summary>
        <div>
            <p>Credits are digital units that allow you to use the AI chatbot. The base price depends on the selected model, and supported optional reasoning can add a surcharge:</p>
            <%= render 'legal_pages/chatbot_pricing_table', locale: :en %>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>How many free credits do I receive?</summary>
        <div><p>Every new user receives <strong><%= RegistrationsController::STARTER_CREDITS %> free starter credits</strong> upon registration. Additional credits can be purchased. Genius, Mastermind and Omniscient require a Pro subscription.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Do credits expire?</summary>
            <p>No. All credits are permanent and never expire, regardless of whether they come from your monthly Pro allocation, purchased packs, or starter credits.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Can I get a refund on credits?</summary>
        <div><p>Credits are non-refundable. If a payment is refunded or charged back, the credits granted by that payment are clawed back proportionally; the balance can temporarily go negative and is settled against later purchases. In the event of a technical error causing credits to be deducted incorrectly, you can contact us at <a href="mailto:info@wetwijzer.be">info@wetwijzer.be</a> and we will manually credit them back.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>What payment methods are accepted?</summary>
        <div><p>Common payment methods are offered through Mollie, including Bancontact, debit and credit cards, and other European payment methods. We do not store card or bank details; payment is processed in Mollie's secure checkout.</p></div>
    </details>

